WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.101 --> 00:00:03.269
-My first guest is an
Emmy-and Tony-nominated actor

00:00:03.269 --> 00:00:06.406
who stars
in the Disney+ series "Loki,"

00:00:06.406 --> 00:00:10.476
which has its season finale
this Wednesday.

00:00:10.476 --> 00:00:13.245
Here is Tom Hiddleston!

00:00:13.245 --> 00:00:15.482
Yeah!
That's what I'm talking about!

00:00:15.482 --> 00:00:18.250
Yes! That's what
I'm talking about!

00:00:18.250 --> 00:00:20.719
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:20.719 --> 00:00:22.922
Come on, now.
That's a stud. Look at that.

00:00:22.922 --> 00:00:25.724
Come on, buddy.
Nice to see you. They love you.

00:00:25.724 --> 00:00:27.660
Oh, my God. Tom --

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:29.261
-Hi, Jimmy.

00:00:29.261 --> 00:00:31.664
-Tom, we have a full audience,
finally.

00:00:31.664 --> 00:00:33.265
And so that's why
they were going crazy.

00:00:33.265 --> 00:00:34.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:36.068
We love you, bud.

00:00:36.068 --> 00:00:38.371
Thank you for
coming on our show.

00:00:38.371 --> 00:00:39.739
We appreciate it, buddy.

00:00:39.739 --> 00:00:41.240
Where are you right now?

00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:43.542
-I'm in London.
-Okay.

00:00:43.542 --> 00:00:44.978
Oh, thank you for doing this.

00:00:44.978 --> 00:00:48.080
It must be either late or early.
So thank you.

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:50.116
-You know, it's fine,
It's like 10:00.

00:00:50.116 --> 00:00:51.784
10:00 is fine.

00:00:51.784 --> 00:00:53.253
-10:00 is fine.
Yeah. Absolutely good.

00:00:53.253 --> 00:00:55.788
I'm happy you're here.
Last time you were on the show,

00:00:55.788 --> 00:00:56.990
we actually were --

00:00:56.990 --> 00:00:59.325
We announced, I think,
that you were going to

00:00:59.325 --> 00:01:02.194
bring "Loki" --
to do "Loki" again.

00:01:02.194 --> 00:01:04.330
Before that, you thought
that it was the end.

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:06.865
You've done --
Your "Loki" days were over.

00:01:06.865 --> 00:01:08.300
-I did -- Well, first of all,

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:11.070
I remember exactly
coming onto a show

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:13.773
and you being, I think,
pretty much the first person

00:01:13.773 --> 00:01:16.609
to announce that it was
happening, and you were so kind.

00:01:16.609 --> 00:01:18.777
And I appreciate it.

00:01:18.777 --> 00:01:21.080
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:23.115
But, yes, I --

00:01:23.115 --> 00:01:26.018
[ Applause ]

00:01:26.018 --> 00:01:27.854
I really did think
it was the end.

00:01:27.854 --> 00:01:30.422
I mean, I thought it was the end
a couple of times, to be honest.

00:01:30.422 --> 00:01:33.259
There was once after
"Thor: The Dark World"

00:01:33.259 --> 00:01:35.728
and then after
"Avengers: Infinity War,"

00:01:35.728 --> 00:01:39.398
which you'll remember the
opening few minutes of that film

00:01:39.398 --> 00:01:41.634
felt pretty conclusive.

00:01:41.634 --> 00:01:43.569
Um...

00:01:43.569 --> 00:01:45.571
-That's a great way to put it.
Yeah. I would say so.

00:01:45.571 --> 00:01:48.140
-It's kind of hard
to come back from that.

00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:50.209
-Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.
You'd think so.

00:01:50.209 --> 00:01:52.779
-Big purple guy with
the big glove and, you know --

00:01:52.779 --> 00:01:55.381
Anyway, they -- There was
a big round of applause on set

00:01:55.381 --> 00:01:57.950
and lots of lovely notes
from the studio saying,

00:01:57.950 --> 00:02:00.954
you know, "We love you, Tom,
and come and see us any time.

00:02:00.954 --> 00:02:02.655
You'll always be part
of the family."

00:02:02.655 --> 00:02:06.291
And I hung up my boots
and said goodbye.

00:02:06.291 --> 00:02:08.094
-It was a proper goodbye.

00:02:08.094 --> 00:02:10.162
-Yeah.
-And then couple years later --

00:02:10.162 --> 00:02:13.232
-Yeah.
That's the thing about Loki,

00:02:13.232 --> 00:02:15.868
is he just --
What do they say about Loki?

00:02:15.868 --> 00:02:21.640
He's like, "I'm Loki,
and when I die, I don't."

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:24.277
-For anyone who hasn't seen --

00:02:24.277 --> 00:02:26.979
There's five episodes out,
correct right now?

00:02:26.979 --> 00:02:28.548
For anyone who hasn't seen this,

00:02:28.548 --> 00:02:31.684
can you explain
the premise of "Loki"?

00:02:31.684 --> 00:02:34.587
-Yes. Okay. Great idea.
Very briefly.

00:02:34.587 --> 00:02:36.923
-I'm gonna leave
the heavy lifting to you, yeah.

00:02:36.923 --> 00:02:38.591
-[ Laughs ] Okay.

00:02:38.591 --> 00:02:42.261
So, in "Avengers: Endgame,"
you'll remember

00:02:42.261 --> 00:02:47.166
the Avengers from 2019
go back in time to 2012.

00:02:47.166 --> 00:02:52.972
And there's a whole situation
with two Tony Starks.

00:02:52.972 --> 00:02:54.406
Antman is there.

00:02:54.406 --> 00:02:57.443
And they make The Hulk
take the stairs.

00:02:57.443 --> 00:03:03.415
And he burst through a hallway
and bumps into 2019 Tony.

00:03:03.415 --> 00:03:07.019
And the suitcase
with the Tesseract goes flying.

00:03:07.019 --> 00:03:08.888
-Yes. That's it. Yes.

00:03:08.888 --> 00:03:10.556
-And he picks up the Tesseract,

00:03:10.556 --> 00:03:12.558
and he disappears
in a puff of smoke.

00:03:12.558 --> 00:03:15.962
And where he goes next
is where we start.

00:03:15.962 --> 00:03:17.763
And he sort of improvises
for a bit.

00:03:17.763 --> 00:03:21.000
And then he's apprehended
by this organization

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:23.903
called the TVA,
which is an organization

00:03:23.903 --> 00:03:27.973
that claims to govern
the order of time.

00:03:27.973 --> 00:03:30.075
But maybe the most important
information you need to know

00:03:30.075 --> 00:03:33.146
is that Owen Wilson
is an analyst for the TVA.

00:03:33.146 --> 00:03:36.983
-That's correct.
You guys are fantastic together.

00:03:36.983 --> 00:03:39.852
Owen Wil--
You guys are great together.

00:03:39.852 --> 00:03:41.253
-Thank you.
-Did you --

00:03:41.253 --> 00:03:43.222
Have you worked together before?

00:03:43.222 --> 00:03:46.492
-Yes, we worked together
in "Midnight in Paris," yeah,

00:03:46.492 --> 00:03:48.327
but this is the first, like,

00:03:48.327 --> 00:03:52.231
really extensive --
Really extensive.

00:03:52.231 --> 00:03:55.267
We did like -- We made this show
across the pandemic

00:03:55.267 --> 00:03:57.103
and got to know each other
very well.

00:03:57.103 --> 00:03:58.771
And he is just great.

00:03:58.771 --> 00:04:00.372
It was one of those things
that was meant to be.

00:04:00.372 --> 00:04:03.276
So, he plays Mobius,
and Mobius is somebody

00:04:03.276 --> 00:04:07.280
who is, like, an academic
and he's an expert in Loki

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:09.649
and he knows more
about Loki than Loki.

00:04:09.649 --> 00:04:16.188
And we have these really amazing
long scenes together

00:04:16.188 --> 00:04:19.825
where Mobius confronts Loki
with his true self

00:04:19.825 --> 00:04:23.796
and almost sees him without
judgment and with compassion.

00:04:23.796 --> 00:04:25.264
It's kind of confronting
for Loki

00:04:25.264 --> 00:04:26.932
because he's normally
used to everybody

00:04:26.932 --> 00:04:28.801
being kind of
emotionally involved.

00:04:28.801 --> 00:04:31.370
Like, Thor was like --
gets enraged by Loki.

00:04:31.370 --> 00:04:33.172
And Odin gets enraged by Loki.

00:04:33.172 --> 00:04:37.076
And Mobius is like...

00:04:37.076 --> 00:04:38.778
-Exactly right. Yeah.

00:04:38.778 --> 00:04:41.246
-But it was cool.
It was like, you know --

00:04:41.246 --> 00:04:44.082
It was like a big -- It was like
a game of tennis every time

00:04:44.082 --> 00:04:45.818
because we had these
long scenes together,

00:04:45.818 --> 00:04:47.653
and we used to talk about,
you know,

00:04:47.653 --> 00:04:50.622
put a different sort of spin
on the ball.

00:04:50.622 --> 00:04:53.625
And in the end,
we talked about it so much

00:04:53.625 --> 00:04:56.461
we had to actually play
some tennis.

00:04:56.461 --> 00:04:59.498
-Did you actually play tennis?

00:04:59.498 --> 00:05:01.934
-Yeah. Yeah.
-Can Owen play?

00:05:01.934 --> 00:05:05.671
-Uh, he certainly can.

00:05:05.671 --> 00:05:08.540
And I don't know.
I somehow thought, like --

00:05:08.540 --> 00:05:11.344
Maybe I just knew
he'd be an athlete.

00:05:11.344 --> 00:05:16.916
But I didn't quite expect the
level of control on the ball.

00:05:16.916 --> 00:05:19.952
If this is an exclusive,
Owen Wilson is --

00:05:19.952 --> 00:05:21.520
I lost,
is what I'm trying to say.

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:23.422
-Okay. Yeah, yeah.

00:05:23.422 --> 00:05:25.624
It doesn't really --
It doesn't matter.

00:05:25.624 --> 00:05:27.927
You guys are fantastic
on the screen together.

00:05:27.927 --> 00:05:29.828
And Disney+
never fools around.

00:05:29.828 --> 00:05:31.931
They always --
You get above and beyond

00:05:31.931 --> 00:05:34.100
with every script
and everything they do.

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:36.635
I will say
the effects are amazing.

00:05:36.635 --> 00:05:40.173
These are movies that
are on your -- your streaming.

00:05:40.173 --> 00:05:45.945
-This is -- We met a bunch
of new Lokis this last week,

00:05:45.945 --> 00:05:49.147
and one was Alligator Loki.

00:05:49.147 --> 00:05:50.749
This is Alligator Loki.

00:05:50.749 --> 00:05:53.585
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:53.585 --> 00:05:56.421
But then we got the exclusive.

00:05:56.421 --> 00:05:59.659
This is what you were
acting with on set.

00:06:01.427 --> 00:06:04.197
This is the Alligator Loki
that we were using.

00:06:04.197 --> 00:06:06.798
-[ Laughs ] Yes.

00:06:06.798 --> 00:06:09.168
-Is it hard to work with that?

00:06:09.168 --> 00:06:10.536
-I mean, look at him.

00:06:10.536 --> 00:06:13.505
A huge star. He's not even
getting up out of his chair.

00:06:13.505 --> 00:06:15.240
[ Laughter ]

00:06:15.240 --> 00:06:17.810
You know, he's like, "Yep,
I'm here," you know,

00:06:17.810 --> 00:06:19.111
"When do you need me?

00:06:19.111 --> 00:06:21.246
Are you ready
for my close-up yet?

00:06:21.246 --> 00:06:23.449
-Yeah. "Hurry up."
Yeah, "We're losing light,"

00:06:23.449 --> 00:06:25.684
stuff like that.
-It actually was funny,

00:06:25.684 --> 00:06:28.254
because, obviously,
he's made out of

00:06:28.254 --> 00:06:31.357
sort of these three
discarded cushions

00:06:31.357 --> 00:06:34.894
sewn up with some eyes on.

00:06:34.894 --> 00:06:37.029
And we would -- I would --

00:06:37.029 --> 00:06:38.864
I mean, I have to --
Like, no offense

00:06:38.864 --> 00:06:42.735
to Alligator Loki,
clearly the superior Loki,

00:06:42.735 --> 00:06:45.470
but I would sometimes --
You'd be doing a scene,

00:06:45.470 --> 00:06:47.573
and you'd think, "Okay,

00:06:47.573 --> 00:06:48.907
so, we're going
to get the wide shot

00:06:48.907 --> 00:06:51.109
and then the two shot,
and we'll do Owen's coverage,

00:06:51.109 --> 00:06:53.779
and get everyone's close-ups
and coverage."

00:06:53.779 --> 00:06:55.381
And you think,
"Okay, I think that was --

00:06:55.381 --> 00:06:57.382
That felt like a great scene.
I think we're done.

00:06:57.382 --> 00:06:59.118
I think we -- Are we moving on?"

00:06:59.118 --> 00:07:00.152
And we'd all sort of wrap --

00:07:00.152 --> 00:07:01.587
"Ah, guys,
that was a great scene.

00:07:01.587 --> 00:07:03.121
It was a great scene.
See you tomorrow."

00:07:03.121 --> 00:07:04.891
And somebody would say,
"Hang on a second.

00:07:04.891 --> 00:07:05.991
We have to shoot --

00:07:05.991 --> 00:07:08.460
We have to shoot
the, uh -- the alligator."

00:07:08.460 --> 00:07:10.529
[ Laughter ]

00:07:10.529 --> 00:07:12.731
-Forget he was there. We shot --
"Sorry, yeah."

00:07:12.731 --> 00:07:15.934
I put my microphone back on.

00:07:15.934 --> 00:07:17.369
-"The alligator
wants one more take.

00:07:17.369 --> 00:07:18.504
Okay, no problem."

00:07:18.504 --> 00:07:21.040
-"You know, uh, yeah,
sun's going down."

00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:23.609
-There's other Loki news
I want to quickly discuss.

00:07:23.609 --> 00:07:27.279
One is, we're big fan of
"The Simpsons" here on our show.

00:07:27.279 --> 00:07:29.982
And they did a short film

00:07:29.982 --> 00:07:32.351
of "The Simpsons"-"Loki"
crossover

00:07:32.351 --> 00:07:34.619
that is fascinating
that you can see on Disney+.

00:07:34.619 --> 00:07:35.788
It's streaming right now.

00:07:35.788 --> 00:07:37.823
It's called "The Good, the Bart,
and the Loki."

00:07:37.823 --> 00:07:39.391
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:39.391 --> 00:07:40.693
And it is --

00:07:40.693 --> 00:07:41.861
-Right there.

00:07:41.861 --> 00:07:43.362
-How is it
working with those guys?

00:07:43.362 --> 00:07:45.297
They're brilliant, right?
They know what they're doing.

00:07:45.297 --> 00:07:47.499
-I have to tell you, Jimmy
I mean, honestly, like,

00:07:47.499 --> 00:07:48.867
I grew up on that show.

00:07:48.867 --> 00:07:52.238
I mean, if I could
go back in time and --

00:07:52.238 --> 00:07:54.039
-Yeah, you can!

00:07:54.039 --> 00:07:55.874
You can!

00:07:55.874 --> 00:07:57.109
You're Loki!

00:07:57.109 --> 00:07:59.145
You can go back in time!
-I can just go back.

00:07:59.145 --> 00:08:01.880
-Yes! Do this! You must go back
and tell yourself

00:08:01.880 --> 00:08:03.415
what you're doing now.

00:08:03.415 --> 00:08:04.784
[ Laughter, applause ]

00:08:04.784 --> 00:08:08.487
-Well, you know, 10-year-old Tom
would be doing back flips

00:08:08.487 --> 00:08:12.224
that he is in a scene
with Homer Simpson.

00:08:12.224 --> 00:08:14.793
-Yeah.
-I mean, look. He's like --

00:08:14.793 --> 00:08:16.161
I can't believe it
when I watch it

00:08:16.161 --> 00:08:19.865
that I'm in a scene
with Homer. And Bart. And Lisa.

00:08:19.865 --> 00:08:21.333
-Yeah. It's wild.

00:08:21.333 --> 00:08:23.436
-But it's great.
It's such an honor.

00:08:23.436 --> 00:08:25.938
I mean, they are --
they are geniuses,

00:08:25.938 --> 00:08:29.742
and it's really, really fun.
-There's also a thing called

00:08:29.742 --> 00:08:31.676
"What If...?"
which is coming out

00:08:31.676 --> 00:08:33.912
for any Marvel fans out there.
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:08:33.912 --> 00:08:36.648
-And basically, it is --
it's animated,

00:08:36.648 --> 00:08:38.483
but basically is that.

00:08:38.483 --> 00:08:40.152
What if "blank" happened?

00:08:40.152 --> 00:08:43.989
What if these people
were never --

00:08:43.989 --> 00:08:45.958
they never fought?
These people were friends?

00:08:45.958 --> 00:08:47.860
What if --
-That's right. Yeah.

00:08:47.860 --> 00:08:50.529
So, I think it was based on
a run of comics

00:08:50.529 --> 00:08:51.998
that actually were released
or published.

00:08:51.998 --> 00:08:57.202
And it's like, what if,
you know, Loki wasn't adopted?

00:08:57.202 --> 00:09:01.507
What if Peggy Carter
was the one who got the serum?

00:09:01.507 --> 00:09:04.876
What if the Ravagers
kidnapped T'Challa

00:09:04.876 --> 00:09:06.679
instead of Peter Quill?

00:09:06.679 --> 00:09:09.948
It's kind of, what if
some major event in history

00:09:09.948 --> 00:09:11.850
had actually gone the other way,

00:09:11.850 --> 00:09:15.220
and what reality
would we be living in now?

00:09:15.220 --> 00:09:18.023
And it's kind of
a great premise, like --

00:09:18.023 --> 00:09:20.158
-Yeah, they're really
doing it up.

00:09:20.158 --> 00:09:22.227
-Yeah. So they've made --

00:09:22.227 --> 00:09:25.398
-Disney gave us
an exclusive shot of Loki,

00:09:25.398 --> 00:09:26.632
what you look like
in "What If...?"

00:09:26.632 --> 00:09:28.600
And here it is right here.
We're debuting this.

00:09:28.600 --> 00:09:30.169
Thank you, Disney.

00:09:30.169 --> 00:09:32.138
There you go.
-There you go.

00:09:32.138 --> 00:09:34.606
-That's an exclusive
right there. Yeah.

00:09:34.606 --> 00:09:38.177
This is exciting.
This is all Loki all the time.

00:09:38.177 --> 00:09:39.845
-I -- [ Laughs ]

00:09:39.845 --> 00:09:42.047
Well, I actually
haven't seen that.

00:09:42.047 --> 00:09:44.950
Um --
[ Laughter ]

00:09:44.950 --> 00:09:47.786
-Loki, yes, you have.

00:09:47.786 --> 00:09:49.755
You were back in time
at one point,

00:09:49.755 --> 00:09:52.724
and you saw.
-And I drew it myself.

00:09:52.724 --> 00:09:54.960
[ Laughter ]

00:09:54.960 --> 00:09:57.463
Just said, "Look, this guy
needs his own animated show."

00:09:57.463 --> 00:10:01.533
The best thing about that
is that I didn't have to get up

00:10:01.533 --> 00:10:04.869
and wear
all that metal and leather.

00:10:04.869 --> 00:10:07.672
-Yeah, yeah. That was all voice.

00:10:07.672 --> 00:10:09.107
-There's a microphone,
and it's like,

00:10:09.107 --> 00:10:12.043
"Oh, I think I can -- This is --
I think this is good.

00:10:12.043 --> 00:10:14.246
This is going to be fun."

00:10:14.246 --> 00:10:16.214
But I am intrigued, 'cause
I haven't seen the whole thing,

00:10:16.214 --> 00:10:19.118
and I know they've got like --
They've got everybody

00:10:19.118 --> 00:10:23.422
from the Marvel Universe
to voice their characters.

00:10:23.422 --> 00:10:25.724
And Jeffrey Wright --
Do you know Jeffrey Wright,

00:10:25.724 --> 00:10:27.159
the great Jeffrey Wright?
-Yes. I love him.

00:10:27.159 --> 00:10:30.262
-He is playing this character
called The Watcher,

00:10:30.262 --> 00:10:34.499
who is sort of an observer of
all of these different things.

00:10:34.499 --> 00:10:37.703
And then it sets up a whole
bunch of stuff in the MCU

00:10:37.703 --> 00:10:41.306
which I know nothing about
and --

00:10:41.306 --> 00:10:43.408
-That's the norm. You're
not allowed to say anything.

00:10:43.408 --> 00:10:45.211
The finale of "Loki,"

00:10:45.211 --> 00:10:47.179
which, by the way,
has been the show of the summer,

00:10:47.179 --> 00:10:50.382
is this Wednesday night.
You set it up now.

00:10:50.382 --> 00:10:51.917
There's a bunch of -- We realize

00:10:51.917 --> 00:10:54.687
there is a bunch
of different Lokis.

00:10:54.687 --> 00:10:58.056
Can you set up anything for what
we're about to see Wednesday?

00:10:58.056 --> 00:11:00.826
And I'm assuming you can't.
But can you?

00:11:00.826 --> 00:11:02.928
[ Laughter ]

00:11:02.928 --> 00:11:04.963
-[ Chuckles ]

00:11:04.963 --> 00:11:06.899
Jimmy, come on, man. I --

00:11:06.899 --> 00:11:08.333
-I know.

00:11:08.333 --> 00:11:10.468
-Yeah. But -- Well,
I suppose I can tell you

00:11:10.468 --> 00:11:13.105
is if you've followed the show
thus far...

00:11:15.608 --> 00:11:16.908
You know, I think
the audience --

00:11:16.908 --> 00:11:20.145
Well, all the characters
and the audience

00:11:20.145 --> 00:11:25.317
have a number of questions
about this TVA,

00:11:25.317 --> 00:11:26.952
the Time Variance Authority,

00:11:26.952 --> 00:11:29.154
like, who made it?

00:11:29.154 --> 00:11:31.156
What is it? Who runs it?

00:11:31.156 --> 00:11:33.292
-Yes.
-Is it run by anyone

00:11:33.292 --> 00:11:34.793
or anything?
-Wow. Yes.

00:11:34.793 --> 00:11:37.395
-Who created it?
-Yes.

00:11:37.395 --> 00:11:40.332
Yes!
-And all I can say --

00:11:40.332 --> 00:11:42.634
-Wow! You're saying a lot.

00:11:42.634 --> 00:11:44.170
[ Laughter ]

00:11:46.338 --> 00:11:47.672
-Time will tell.

00:11:47.672 --> 00:11:49.774
-Whoa! That's what
I'm talking about.

00:11:49.774 --> 00:11:51.644
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:11:51.644 --> 00:11:55.480
That's exactly what you want
to hear. "Time will tell."

00:11:55.480 --> 00:11:58.551
Mm. I'm going to figure out
what that means.

00:11:58.551 --> 00:11:59.852
-You will.
-Tom Hiddleston, everybody,

00:11:59.852 --> 00:12:01.420
the one and only.

00:12:01.420 --> 00:12:03.588
The season finale of "Loki"
is available this Wednesday

00:12:03.588 --> 00:12:04.824
on Disney+.

